## 1. Built
- **`crates/umber-app/src/viewport.rs`** (only file changed, +74/−6): the CORE-LOOP viewport texture binding.
  - `Viewport::ui` frame path: `if let Some(mesh) = &self.mesh` → `self.mesh.as_mut()`, and `bind_paint_target(gpu, mesh, paint.as_deref())` runs before either route arm builds its callback, so Direct **and** PostFx frames (PostFx reuses the mesh's own callback internally) see paint.
  - New free fn `bind_paint_target`: active tile via `paint.active_tile()` + `paint.tile_target(tile)` → `mesh.set_base_color_texture(gpu, target, PaintParams::for_udim(tile))`; `None` session or missing tile → `mesh.clear_base_color_texture(gpu)` (fallback arm; mesh-less hero path binds nothing, pixel-identical).
  - Borrow fix: the paint-input branch `(self.mesh_data.as_ref(), paint)` **moved** `paint`; now `paint.as_mut()` (+ `mut` on the param — the contract's E0596 trap, which clippy caught once), keeping it alive for the bind.
  - `post.callback(gpu, mesh…)` / `wire_callback(mesh…)` call sites adjusted to `&*mesh`.
- **`crates/umber-app/src/main.rs`**: read, verified, **untouched** — `PanelViewer` already passes `self.paint.as_deref_mut()` at :144 and `viewport.ui`'s signature is unchanged, so the borrow flow needed nothing structural.
- Tests added: **0** — per the brief, the golden safety is existing tests passing unchanged plus the renderer's own tests (the app has no GPU golden for the viewport; `bind_paint_target` needs a live device and can't run headless).

## 2. Judgment calls (all also in `viewport.rs` module docs + `bind_paint_target` docs)
- **Bind the active tile, not hardcoded 1001.** Single-tile sessions always have active == 1001 (behavior unchanged); multi-tile shows the tile under the last pointer. The atlas + page-table (all tiles at once) is the documented later slice. Renderer docs prescribe exactly this ("the app binds the active tile's `PaintTarget`").
- **Real API is `PaintParams::for_udim(tile)`** — the brief's `for_tile(tile_index, mesh_tiles)` doesn't exist. Imported as `umber_gpu::renderer::PaintParams` (`PaintParams` is not re-exported at the crate root; precedent: `main.rs`'s `umber_gpu::renderer::depth_format()`). UV derivation: offset `((tile−1001)%10, (tile−1001)/10)`, scale 1 — the exact inverse of `paint_state`'s `local_texel` offsets (verified by reading both); no target size enters the bind (shader samples UV space).
- **Rebind every frame while paint is present.** `Resize` replaces the tile's texture object (`paint_thread.rs:245`), so a params-equality skip would sample the evicted texture. Cost: one bind group + one small uniform write/frame. The `clear` path *is* skipped when already cleared (`flags == 0` holds no view — provably identical).
- No requirements-row mark: this is one link of the core-loop phase, not a completed row.

